{"event": "report", "t": 1795261868.257, "claim": "fixed", "text": "eriod` model reads from a different source, so I left it alone.\n\n**What I built** (in `/app/dbt_project`):\n- `dbt_project.yml`, `profiles.yml` (profile `retail_dw_master`, DuckDB target writing to schema `analytics`, plus a Snowflake target that reads the `SNOWFLAKE_*` env vars and sets `schema` from `SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA`), and `models/sources.yml`.\n- `models/marts/marketing/rpt_cac_payback_waterfall_fixed.sql`.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- **Channel key:** each campaign's `channel_key` is the one with the highest total spend. Ties go to the lower key, so the result is deterministic.\n- **Daily rows:** I aggregate spend and revenue per campaign per day, and only days with source data get a row. I did not fill gaps between observed days.\n- **Rounding:** cumulative totals are summed from unrounded values and rounded only at output. Rounding each day first would drift past the 0.01 reconciliation tolerance.\n- **Payback:** `payback_ratio` is cumulative revenue \u00f7 cumulative spend. `is_paid_back` is true when cumulative revenue \u2265 cumulative spend.\n\n**Verification (DuckDB):**\n- `dbt run` completed with PASS=1.\n- Column types match the spec.\n- 994 rows across 30 campaigns, one per campaign-day. The row count is below the source's 1,000 because six campaign-days appear under two channels and were merged; the distinct campaign-day count in the source is also 994.\n- Exactly one `channel_key` per campaign, and no duplicate `(campaign_id, days_since_cohort)` pairs.\n- One cohort row (day 0) per campaign.\n- No negative values, and cumulative spend and revenue never decrease within a campaign.\n- For all 30 campaigns, the last-row cumulative totals match source totals within 0.01.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- `profiles.yml` lives in `/app/dbt_project`, so run dbt with `--profiles-dir /app/dbt_project`. I did not copy it to `~/.dbt/`.\n- The Snowflake target is configured but untested. The SQL has a small Jinja branch for the date parse, so it should work there, but I have not run it.\n\nVERDICT: fixed", "verdict": null}
